+
+I'll first look at the failing code path. In `src/_pytest/assertion/rewrite.py`, the `run()` method treats any first `ast.Expr` whose value is an `ast.Constant` as a potential docstring, then calls `is_rewrite_disabled(doc)` which does `"PYTEST_DONT_REWRITE" in docstring`. If the first statement is a number (e.g. `123`), `doc` is an `int`, causing `TypeError: argument of type 'int' is not iterable`.
+
+The fix is to only treat the constant as a docstring when its value is actually a `str`. I'll also add a regression test.
